  "transcriptContext": "Reina’s own spot on our six-handed table: ace-five of spades, A♠ 5♠, dealt to you on the button, with every player sitting on 1,000. As she says the first player to enter the pot, the blinds post 5 and 10, the table’s own blinds for this lesson, so the pot reads 15; Reina names no blind, stack, open size or range width. As she says when everyone folds to you, under the gun, middle position and the cutoff fold, and the action waits on you. As she talks about early position, the under the gun tag and the five seats that act after it light; as she talks about late position, the cutoff and the button light, then the two blinds, the only players left behind you. The suited ace lights as she names it, the ace as she says it blocks strong aces, both spades as she says the nut flush, and the button as she says it gets to act last. No action is taken for you and none is recommended on screen: the decision is left to you in the hand that follows. The other players’ cards stay face down and no flop is dealt. The original voice and speaking animation play continuously at their original speed.",
